<title>TURKEY: Turkish Aksa to give rights, bonuses.</title>
<headline>Turkish Aksa to give rights, bonuses.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish acrylic based tow and fibre producer Aksa Akrilik Kimya Sanayii A.S. decided to increase its capital to 5,675.1 billion lira from 3,338.3 billion, the Istanbul Stock Exchange reported.</p>
<p>The company plans to issue 1,669 billion lira of rights, or 0.50-for-one existing share and 667.7 billion lira of bonuses, or 0.20-for-one existing share after securing approval from Turkey's regulatory Capital Markets Board (SPK).</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
